  {
   "topic": "Windings",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two coupled windings share one ferrite core. Pins 1 to 2 are one winding and pins 4 to 3 the other, with pins 1 and 4 marked as the same-phase ends."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Choosing a value",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moving up the series from -251 to -222 raises inductance (18 to 150 nH min), common-mode impedance and low-frequency common-mode attenuation, and lowers the differential -3 dB cutoff from 3.8 GHz to 0.96 GHz and raises DCR from 0.077 to 0.209 Ohm. The -222 gives 20.29 dB typical common-mode attenuation at 1 GHz. All five carry 500 mA per winding and are isolated to 250 Vrms."
  },
